# Build context for the single-container image (Dockerfile at the repo root).
#
# Two jobs. The obvious one is keeping the context small — `.git` and three
# node_modules trees are most of a gigabyte and none of it reaches the image.
#
# The other is a Docker bug this project has already been bitten by, recorded in
# CLAUDE.md: on this Docker version a build context containing BOTH a root
# dotfile and a subdirectory fails outright with "changes out of order". It is
# why the api and web builds use ./backend and ./frontend as their contexts
# rather than the repository root. This image needs both directories, so it has
# to use the root — and every root dotfile is excluded below to stay clear of it.

.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.dockerignore
.env
.env.*
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Not built into this image.
homeops-mobile/
backups/
docs/
scripts/
*.md

# Read out of band by the client, so excluding them from the context loses
# nothing and keeps the walk a little smaller.
#
# It does NOT fix `docker compose build` on Docker Desktop for Windows, which
# fails with `changes out of order: "backend/alembic.ini"` while `docker build .`
# on the identical context succeeds every time. Things tried and ruled out:
# pruning the builder cache, COMPOSE_BAKE=false, removing the explicit
# `dockerfile:` key, eliminating the two-`docker/`-directories path collision,
# and an uppercase drive letter. Cause unknown. See the note in
# docker-compose.single.yml for the two-step build that does work.
Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml

# Never useful in an image, and node_modules would be copied *over* the one
# `npm install` creates in the build stage.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.venv
venv/
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
# An editable install leaves this in backend/src; it must not reach the image,
# where pip does its own install.
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# The suite runs against the dev stack, not this image.
backend/tests
